  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which 9-Angeloylretronecine may interact with the High-affinity choline transporter. This compound is implicated in the targeting of Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Ancistrobenomine A, Petroraspailyne B1, and Interiorin. All of these agents are linked to the High-affinity choline transporter, indicating a common pathway where 9-Angeloylretronecine may exert its effects through the same or related molecular mechanisms. The scores across the three paths are consistent, suggesting a plausible and well-supported relationship. The mechanism appears to involve the inhibition or modulation of a key enzyme in the choline transport pathway, potentially through the interaction with Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between 9-Angeloylretronecine and the High-affinity choline transporter, with the core pathway involving the demethylase enzyme and its downstream effects on choline transport.",
